WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.835
The second group
of Democratic candidates

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.671
squared off for day two
of their primary debate.

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:08.608
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.345
♪♪

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:15.248
As this debate was going on, the
President was out of the country

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.717
for the G-20 Summit,
where he's been weighing in

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.318
with his usual Twitter nonsense,

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.854
but after he landed in Alaska
to meet with troops,

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:24.791
he couldn't help but comment
to reporters in person.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.792
-Good timing.
The debate is going on.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.261
This is great timing.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.728
-What are your expectations?

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:32.097
-I think they're all
going to do very poorly.

00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:34.033
-I'm sorry, but why are we even

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.336
asking Trump
for his take on this?

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.971
There are a million other
questions you can ask him.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.474
Don't ask him
"man on the street" stuff.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:45.144
"Sir, are you excited
for the new 'Toy Story' movie?"

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.080
Beside, what do you think
he's going to say?

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.148
"I'm very excited.
I love Elizabeth Warren.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:54.020
And I think Tim Ryan's eyes
will look totally normal."

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.988
Also, you think
they're going to do poorly?

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:58.390
Be careful for what you
wish for, dude, because judging

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.760
recent history,
doing poorly at debates

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.596
is a pretty good indicator
of future success.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.199
Maybe one of the Democrats...

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.137
Maybe one of the Democrats
should take a cue from you

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.406
and stalk the other nine
around the debate stage

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.175
like an extra
from "The Walking Dead."

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:17.477
Now, as we mentioned yesterday,

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.145
Elizabeth Warren's
rise in the polls

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.479
has caught the attention of both

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:22.448
Democratic front-runner
Joe Biden and Trump,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.682
and that hasn't stopped Trump

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:25.651
from attacking the other
candidates, as well,

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:26.886
like Biden and Bernie Sanders,

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.454
as he did in an interview
last week.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.189
-Who would you prefer
as an adversary?

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.058
-You know,
I've been asked that question.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:35.127
Honestly, you never know.
You never know.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.430
I could comment
on different ones,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.964
but I won't bother too much.

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:44.237
I think Bernie looks like
he's had it.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.505
Bernie looks crazy,
but he always did.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.541
But he looks like
a tired crazy right now.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:52.778
And Joe Biden, he looks like
he's just exhausted.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:55.815
-Oh, I'm sorry.
Biden looks exhausted?

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.983
Whenever you have to stand
for more than five minutes,

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.619
you look like
you're going to tip over

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.221
and fall flat on your face.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.623
This, though --
This is what Trump does.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.658
Trump projects onto other people

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.159
things that are true
about himself.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:09.028
"Bernie's crazy,
Biden's exhausted.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:13.332
And don't get me started
on John Delaney's weird hair."

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:16.101
Now, the debates were sorted
into two groups of ten by random

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:18.470
drawing because there's
so many candidates running.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.340
In fact, in total,
there are 24 Democrats

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.007
running for president.
Look at that.

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:23.810
There are so many people
on the screen,

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.679
you didn't notice that
one of them is Mr. Bean.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:29.015
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.949
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.949 --> 00:02:33.586
And he's very, very good
at debates

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.189
because his answers
are the shortest.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.558
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.298
So, going into
last night's debate,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.234
it was basically just
Warren and nine other people

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.569
trying to stand out,
and to be fair,

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:50.636
a few of them had their moments.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:52.171
But I'm not sure
I necessarily agree

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.540
with this assessment
of Beto O'Rourke's performance

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.842
from Beto O'Rourke.
-How do you think you did

00:02:56.842 --> 00:03:01.314
on the stage last night? What
grade would you give yourself?

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.949
-I was really happy
with how I did.

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:08.187
-Okay, but what grade would you
give yourself for last night?

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.189
-I'd give myself an A.

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:13.659
-No. I'd definitely give you
an A in freshman Spanish.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:16.929
But I think Cory Booker
would disagree.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:21.567
That's the face right there
you make...

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.070
That's the face you make

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.472
when you see someone
trying to cram a suitcase

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.975
that doesn't fit
into the overhead.

00:03:29.975 --> 00:03:32.945
That's the face you make
when a guy gets on the subway

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:35.648
with a pet snake
around his neck.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:40.286
"Uh, is anyone else
seeing this?"

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.588
Then there was New York City
mayor Bill de Blasio,

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:44.723
who brought a very New York vibe
to the debate

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:47.092
by getting into confrontations
with other candidates

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:49.728
and shouting over the moderators
during commercial breaks,

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:52.064
but he at least found
some opportunities to stand out,

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:54.801
and apparently MSNBC host
Chris Matthews noticed

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.869
because he praised de Blasio
after the debate.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.637
-Are you really in this race?
-Yes, sir.

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:00.539
-I thought tonight
for the first time --

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:01.741
I'm being blunt.
-Yeah.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.643
-I felt you were in this fight
for real,

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.677
not just one of the guys
at the end of the row.

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:09.015
I believe in you tonight.
I think you got in the fight.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.249
-It makes sense Chris Matthews

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:11.784
would like a candidate
who fights.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.285
Chris Matthews looks like a guy

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.555
who fights with the toaster
in the break room.

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:20.092
"Give me back my bagel,
ya silver bastard!

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:23.229
Don't make me
put a fork in you!"

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:26.999
But, still,
the striking contrast

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:30.803
between this first debate
and the 2016 GOP debates

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:32.337
was just how civil it was.

00:04:32.337 --> 00:04:35.274
Of course, we all remember
the WWE-style cage match

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.076
that took place four years ago
between Trump

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.277
and the rest of the GOP field.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:40.179
-I would not have nominated
John Roberts.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.747
-You pushed him.
You pushed him.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:43.249
You worked with him,
and you pushed him!

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.551
Why do you lie?
Why do you lie?

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.888
This little guy has lied so much
about my record.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:51.257
-You ever heard of Trump Steaks?

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.726
-You know what? You know what?
Take a look at Trump Steaks.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.861
-People are actually
watching this --

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:58.131
-Gentlemen, gentlemen.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:01.233
-So far, I'm doing better.
You started off over here, Jeb.

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.302
You're moving over
further and further.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:05.137
Pretty soon
you're going to be off the end.

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:08.941
-Now compare that to
the relationship between Warren

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:12.044
and former Housing Secretary
Julian Castro,

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.480
who had a few of his own
standout moments last night.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.250
Here's how Warren responded
to Castro's performance today.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.918
-We're also hearing this morning

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.020
from both the Warren
and Castro camps

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.122
that Warren sent Castro
a text message

00:05:24.122 --> 00:05:25.324
after last night's debate

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.092
telling him that
he did a good job.

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:29.628
-Man, it's amazing
how polite the first debate was

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:31.864
compared to
the 2016 GOP debates.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.333
Can you imagine the text
Trump sent to Jeb Bush?

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:38.771
"Nerd. Loser. Hey, loser.
Respond to me, loser.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.106
No, seriously.
I have a question, Jeb."

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:43.976
"What, Donald?"
"Why are you such a loser?"

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.979
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.280
But the other striking thing --

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.149
and it's crazy that this
is even notable --

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.818
is how truthful
the first debate was.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:53.986
CNN reporter Daniel Dale,
who's well known for

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.622
exhaustively cataloging and
debunking all of Trump's lies

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.724
and even wrote recently
that Donald Trump has now said

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.660
more than 5,000 false things
as President,

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.395
was supposed to
go on CNN last night

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.096
to fact-check
the Democratic debate.

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:05.597
But then after the debate,
he tweeted,

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:07.800
"Well, tonight's candidates
were so heavily factual

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.603
that I will not, in fact,
be going on CNN to
fact-check them."

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:13.172
That's wild.
Fact-checking is the only field

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:17.009
where Donald Trump can actually
say he created more jobs.

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.145
Can you imagine
what CNN's gonna be like

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.579
if a Democrat is president?

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.849
That place is gonna be like
Margaritaville.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.650
Wolf Blitzer's gonna do his show

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.920
sitting in a hammock
drinking a wine cooler.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.224
Now, everyone had different ways
of preparing for these debates.

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:34.326
Coming into tonight, Biden had
attracted the most attention

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:35.995
because he's the front-runner
in the polls,

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:38.297
but a lot of his past policies
and Senate votes are out of step

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.099
with many of today's
Democratic primary voters,

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:43.002
and his rivals have been
pouncing on those positions.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:45.537
So Biden was supposedly trying
to prepare for those attacks

00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:47.005
coming into tonight.

00:06:47.005 --> 00:06:49.675
-Senator Elizabeth Warren
and her 2020 Democratic rivals

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.743
are very busy right now
because they're prepping

00:06:51.743 --> 00:06:53.579
for the first pair
of Democratic debates

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.048
which are tomorrow night
and Thursday night in Miami.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:58.584
And for her part,
Warren has focused on

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.354
boiling down
her policy positions

00:07:01.354 --> 00:07:03.155
to try to fit
the time constraints.

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:06.058
Former vice president Joe Biden
has been studying

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.427
his own record
preparing for attacks on it.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:09.629
-Man, it's not good when you

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.597
have to study your own record
before a debate.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:13.599
That's like when somebody
ghosts you on Tinder,

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.734
and you have to go back
and read your conversation

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.903
to see where you blew it.

00:07:17.903 --> 00:07:19.705
"But we had so much fun.
I don't --

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.875
Oh, I forgot -- I forgot
I said that about her dog.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.443
Okay. That's on me.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:27.113
'Cause that's definitely
where it ended."

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.181
Now, one of the big divides
coming into tonight

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:30.750
was between
progressive candidates

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.651
in favor of policies
like Medicare For All

00:07:32.651 --> 00:07:34.187
and the more moderate
candidates,

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:36.655
like Biden and former Colorado
governor John Hickenlooper,

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:37.990
who has said the Democrats

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.792
shouldn't veer toward socialism.

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.394
Hickenlooper was asked tonight
about that position.

00:07:42.394 --> 00:07:44.330
-Governor Hickenlooper,
let me get you in on this.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.599
You've warned that Democrats
will lose in 2020

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:50.469
if they embrace socialism,
as you put it.

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.238
You were booed at the
California Democratic Convention

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:55.040
when you said that.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.910
Only one candidate on this
stage, Senator Sanders,

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:00.846
identifies himself
as a Democratic Socialist.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.015
What are the policies or
positions of your opponents

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:06.285
that you think are veering
toward socialism?

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:09.455
-Well, I think
that the bottom line is

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:12.358
if we don't clearly define
that we are not socialists,

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:15.027
the Republicans are going to
come at us every way they can

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.929
and call us socialists.

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:19.164
-Hey, man.
Have you met Republicans?

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:22.434
They're going to call you
socialists anyway.

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:25.070
If you go out to dinner
with them and tip more than 10%,

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.739
they'll call you a socialist.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:29.074
Where you been
for the last ten years?

00:08:29.074 --> 00:08:30.809
They called President Obama
a socialist

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:33.011
despite the fact that he is
definitely not a socialist.

00:08:33.011 --> 00:08:35.114
I mean, look at him.
You can't be a socialist

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:37.649
when you look like
you're gonna model

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:41.387
in an ad for TAG Heuer watches.

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:46.191
He looks like he's auditioning
for a remake of "Jerry Maguire."

00:08:46.191 --> 00:08:48.094
And Colorado senator
Michael Bennet

00:08:48.094 --> 00:08:49.529
also tried to take on Bernie

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:51.630
with a dig at his
Medicare For All plan.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.767
-Bernie mentioned that the taxes
that we'd have to pay.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.268
Because of those taxes,

00:08:56.268 --> 00:08:58.604
Vermont rejected
Medicare For All.

00:08:58.604 --> 00:09:01.473
[ Overlapping shouting ]

00:09:01.473 --> 00:09:03.942
-It's amazing how Bernie
can respond to something

00:09:03.942 --> 00:09:05.978
with just a face.

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:08.247
It's like when you take your
iPad out at the dinner table

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:10.382
and your grandpa goes,
"Oh, no, no, no!

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:13.652
The only pads we'll be using
are Brillo Pads.

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:15.921
When we wash the dishes
the old-fashioned way!"

00:09:15.921 --> 00:09:19.458
Then moderators asked a question
they also asked yesterday.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.360
Who would abolish
private health insurance?

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.562
Bernie and Senator Kamala Harris
raised their hands,

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:25.598
and then it seemed like
Biden maybe didn't know

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:27.733
whether he was supposed to
raise his hand or not.

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:30.736
-Who here would abolish
their private health insurance

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:34.506
in favorite of
a government-run plan?

00:09:34.506 --> 00:09:36.342
All right.

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:37.943
[ Applause ]

00:09:37.943 --> 00:09:39.745
Kirsten Gillibrand.

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:43.615
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.615 --> 00:09:45.384
-That's the...

00:09:45.384 --> 00:09:48.353
definition of a centrist
right there.

00:09:48.353 --> 00:09:50.723
And what's up with him sort of
halfway raising his hand?

00:09:50.723 --> 00:09:53.225
That's like in Phys Ed when the
teacher is divvying up the class

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:57.063
and you want to be on a team
with your friend.

00:09:57.063 --> 00:09:58.931
He was also slow
to raise his hand later

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:01.567
when the moderators asked whose
healthcare plans would cover

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:04.236
undocumented immigrants,
prompting some confusion.

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:06.338
-Raise your hand
if your government plan

00:10:06.338 --> 00:10:10.309
would provide coverage
for undocumented immigrants.

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:12.211
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:13.712
-Okay.

00:10:13.712 --> 00:10:15.614
Vice President Biden,
I believe you said

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:17.683
that your healthcare plan
would not cover

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:20.051
undocumented immigrants.
Could you explain your position?

00:10:20.051 --> 00:10:21.520
-I'm sorry.
Beg your pardon?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.788
-I believe,
at the show of hands,

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:25.391
you did not raise your hand.
Did you raise your hand?

00:10:25.391 --> 00:10:27.927
-No, I did.
-Okay, sorry, sorry.

00:10:27.927 --> 00:10:29.161
-"Did you raise your hand?"

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:31.163
"Uh, if I had the right answer,
I did."

00:10:31.163 --> 00:10:32.565
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:35.167
"What was your answer --
or, what was the question?"

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.602
[ Laughter ]

00:10:36.602 --> 00:10:39.771
Then, the issue of age came up
when California Congressman

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:42.107
Eric Swalwell
took a dig at Biden

00:10:42.107 --> 00:10:44.410
using an old quote
from Biden himself.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.346
-I was 6 years old
when a presidential candidate

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:50.249
came to the California
Democratic Convention and said,

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:55.121
"It's time to pass the torch to
a new generation of Americans."

00:10:55.121 --> 00:10:58.090
That candidate
was then-Senator Joe Biden.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.860
Joe Biden was right when he said
it is time to pass the torch

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.329
to a new generation of Americans
32 years ago.

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:05.231
He's still right today.

00:11:05.231 --> 00:11:07.465
If we're gonna solve
the issues of automation,

00:11:07.465 --> 00:11:08.900
pass the torch.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:12.171
-Damn. You're bringing a Biden
quote to take down Biden?

00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:15.907
Come on! If anyone's
gonna take down Joe Biden

00:11:15.907 --> 00:11:18.344
with a Joe Biden quote,
it's Joe Biden.

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:19.711
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.711 --> 00:11:22.047
Also, look at that smile.

00:11:22.047 --> 00:11:23.448
[ Laughter ]

00:11:23.448 --> 00:11:27.119
Joe Biden uses his teeth the way
Wonder Woman uses her bracelets.

00:11:27.119 --> 00:11:28.554
[ Laughter ]

00:11:28.554 --> 00:11:32.491
That zinger just bounced right
off that pearly white wall.

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.126
And by the way, just in case
you were wondering,

00:11:34.126 --> 00:11:36.762
after last night's debate,
another candidate got a chance

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:39.798
to bust out some Spanish again,
and it was South Bend mayor

00:11:39.798 --> 00:11:41.066
Pete Buttigieg.

00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:42.968
-I want to say hello
and good evening.

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:45.804
Buenos noches
to Mayor Buttigieg.

00:11:45.804 --> 00:11:48.907
[ Conversing in Spanish ]

00:11:48.907 --> 00:11:50.809
-When he did that,
NBC took a live shot

00:11:50.809 --> 00:11:52.144
of Cory booker at home.

00:11:52.144 --> 00:11:53.846
[ Laughter ]

00:11:53.846 --> 00:11:56.748
Now, the question of healthcare
was obviously a hot topic,

00:11:56.748 --> 00:11:58.917
as were many questions,
which led to a lot of

00:11:58.917 --> 00:12:00.886
overtalking and yelling
at the beginning.

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:03.922
-On this issue, we have to think
about how this affects...

00:12:03.922 --> 00:12:05.257
[ Overlapping speakers ]

00:12:05.257 --> 00:12:08.160
-Senator Harris --
Senator Harris, I'm so sorry.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.863
-As part of --
As part of Joe's generation --

00:12:11.863 --> 00:12:14.232
-No, I'm all for --
-As part of Joe's generation --

00:12:14.232 --> 00:12:15.601
Let me respond.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.903
-Good Lord. It sounds like
the audience at a cockfight.

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:18.937
[ Laughter ]

00:12:18.937 --> 00:12:20.171
And I'm sorry -- you guys think

00:12:20.171 --> 00:12:22.140
you can win a scream fight
with Bernie Sanders?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.610
You're bringing a kazoo
to a bullhorn fight.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:25.678
[ Laughter ]

00:12:25.678 --> 00:12:27.546
They didn't even turn on
Bernie's mic

00:12:27.546 --> 00:12:29.215
because it would
blow out the speakers.

00:12:29.215 --> 00:12:30.949
[ Laughter ]

00:12:30.949 --> 00:12:32.618
But then, Harris jumped in
with a line

00:12:32.618 --> 00:12:35.588
that got raucous applause
and quieted everyone else down.

00:12:35.588 --> 00:12:38.557
-Senator Harris.
[ Overlapping arguing ]

00:12:38.557 --> 00:12:39.859
-Hey, guys.
You know what?

00:12:39.859 --> 00:12:41.994
America does not
want to witness a food fight.

00:12:41.994 --> 00:12:44.630
They want to know how we're
gonna put food on their table.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:50.402
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:50.402 --> 00:12:52.605
-Damn!
[ Laughter ]

00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:55.073
Look at how sheepish
everyone was after she --

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:56.275
She embarrassed them so badly,

00:12:56.275 --> 00:12:58.344
John Hickenlooper
had to go stand in the corner.

00:12:58.344 --> 00:13:00.679
[ Laughter ]

00:13:00.679 --> 00:13:02.214
Then, there were
the lesser-known candidates,

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:04.282
like former tech executive
Andrew Yang.

00:13:04.282 --> 00:13:05.817
All right, Andrew, you haven't
gotten a lot of coverage,

00:13:05.817 --> 00:13:07.119
you need a breakthrough.
You got to nail it.

00:13:07.119 --> 00:13:09.655
This is your big moment,"
so I'm sure you were ready.

00:13:09.655 --> 00:13:13.992
-Mr. Yang your signature policy
is to give

00:13:13.992 --> 00:13:18.029
every adult in the United States
$1,000 a month,

00:13:18.029 --> 00:13:20.766
no questions asked.
-That's right.

00:13:20.766 --> 00:13:25.804
-I think that's
like $3.2 trillion a year.

00:13:25.804 --> 00:13:27.773
How would you do that?

00:13:27.773 --> 00:13:28.841
-Sorry?

00:13:28.841 --> 00:13:31.676
[ Laughter ]

00:13:31.676 --> 00:13:34.079
-"Just forget it.
Forget it.

00:13:34.079 --> 00:13:37.315
Move on.
How are you not ready?"

00:13:37.315 --> 00:13:39.051
It's like a backup
on Golden State who finally

00:13:39.051 --> 00:13:41.086
gets put in the game
and then just chucks the ball

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:42.521
into the stands
the minute he gets it.

00:13:42.521 --> 00:13:44.189
[ Laughter ]

00:13:44.189 --> 00:13:45.858
But then, one of the biggest
moments of the debate came

00:13:45.858 --> 00:13:48.226
when Harris confronted Biden
about his record on race

00:13:48.226 --> 00:13:49.828
and recent comments
about working

00:13:49.828 --> 00:13:51.496
with segregationist senators.

00:13:51.496 --> 00:13:53.865
-We've also heard --
and I'm gonna now direct this

00:13:53.865 --> 00:13:56.602
at Vice President Biden.

00:13:56.602 --> 00:13:59.070
I do not believe
you are a racist.

00:13:59.070 --> 00:14:03.242
And I agree with you
when you commit yourself

00:14:03.242 --> 00:14:06.177
to the importance
of finding common ground.

00:14:06.177 --> 00:14:08.813
But I also believe --
And it's personal,

00:14:08.813 --> 00:14:11.950
and I was actually very --
It was hurtful

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:15.554
to hear you talk about
the reputations

00:14:15.554 --> 00:14:20.158
of two United States Senators
who built their reputations

00:14:20.158 --> 00:14:24.329
and career on the segregation
of race in this country.

00:14:24.329 --> 00:14:27.633
It cannot be an intellectual
debate among Democrats.

00:14:27.633 --> 00:14:31.436
We have to take it seriously,
we have to act swiftly.

00:14:31.436 --> 00:14:34.206
As Attorney General
of California, I was very proud

00:14:34.206 --> 00:14:37.409
to put in place a requirement
that all my special agents

00:14:37.409 --> 00:14:40.612
would wear body cameras
and keep those cameras on.

00:14:40.612 --> 00:14:42.714
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Senator Harris, thank you.

00:14:42.714 --> 00:14:45.116
Vice President Biden,
you have been invoked.

00:14:45.116 --> 00:14:48.920
We are going to give you
a chance to respond.

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.890
-Even his teeth
couldn't save him from that one.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.426
And it was clear everyone
wanted a shot at Biden tonight.

00:14:54.426 --> 00:14:56.895
Bennet also went after Biden for
previous comments he's made,

00:14:56.895 --> 00:14:58.663
suggesting he'll be able
to work with Republicans

00:14:58.663 --> 00:15:00.098
after Trump leaves office

00:15:00.098 --> 00:15:02.700
and his record of compromising
with Republicans.

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:04.402
-Chuck, the problem with what
the Vice President --

00:15:04.402 --> 00:15:07.306
-30 seconds.
Yeah, 30 seconds, go ahead.

00:15:07.306 --> 00:15:09.775
-Sometimes you do have
to beat them,

00:15:09.775 --> 00:15:12.444
but the deal that he talked
about with Mitch McConnell

00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:15.280
was a complete victory
for the Tea Party.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:19.284
That deal extended almost all
those Bush tax cuts permanently

00:15:19.284 --> 00:15:22.021
and put in place
the mindless cuts

00:15:22.021 --> 00:15:24.356
that we still
are dealing with today

00:15:24.356 --> 00:15:25.991
that are called the sequester.

00:15:25.991 --> 00:15:28.426
That was a great deal
for Mitch McConnell.

00:15:28.426 --> 00:15:30.596
It was a terrible deal
for America.

00:15:30.596 --> 00:15:32.030
-Thank you, Senator Bennet.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.833
-Man, who didn't get a crack
at Biden during this debate?

00:15:34.833 --> 00:15:36.735
I'm surprised one of the
moderators didn't juste go,

00:15:36.735 --> 00:15:38.904
"Hey, man, you were great in
'Grand Torino.'"

00:15:38.904 --> 00:15:40.672
[ Laughter ]

00:15:40.672 --> 00:15:42.574
At some point,
they just started inviting

00:15:42.574 --> 00:15:44.909
random audience members
up on stage to slam him.

00:15:44.909 --> 00:15:47.446
"Uh, yeah, I just want to say
I'm more of a bus guy,

00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:49.080
and I think Amtrak sucks ass!

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.150
[ Laughter ]
Team Greyhound!

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.417
[ Laughter ]

00:15:52.417 --> 00:15:54.353
And Biden seemed kind of
defeated by all the attacks,

00:15:54.353 --> 00:15:56.521
'cause at one point he just said
he was out of time.

00:15:56.521 --> 00:16:00.725
-I'm the guy that extended the
Voting Rights Act for 25 years.

00:16:00.725 --> 00:16:04.029
We got to the place
where we got 98 out of 98 votes

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:05.864
in the United States Senate
doing it.

00:16:05.864 --> 00:16:09.000
I've also argued very strongly
that we, in fact,

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:13.271
deal with the notion of denying
people access to the ballot box.

00:16:13.271 --> 00:16:15.741
I agree that everybody
wants that.

00:16:15.741 --> 00:16:17.476
Anyway, my time's up.
I'm sorry.

00:16:17.476 --> 00:16:19.411
[ Laughter ]

00:16:19.411 --> 00:16:22.247
-Man, you know it's bad when
you're cutting yourself off.

00:16:22.247 --> 00:16:23.481
Also, when everyone's saying
you might be

00:16:23.481 --> 00:16:26.051
too old to be President,
don't say, "My time's up."

00:16:26.051 --> 00:16:28.186
That's like
if Buttigieg had said,

00:16:28.186 --> 00:16:30.389
"It looks like
I'm running short."

00:16:30.389 --> 00:16:32.524
[ Audience groans ]
And once again, of course --

00:16:32.524 --> 00:16:35.761
[ Laughter ]

00:16:35.761 --> 00:16:38.396
While he was at the G20 summit
meeting with world leaders,

00:16:38.396 --> 00:16:40.365
Trump could not help
but comment on the debate.

00:16:40.365 --> 00:16:42.868
Trump reportedly told German
Chancellor Angela Merkel

00:16:42.868 --> 00:16:45.137
he just passed a TV
and saw the debate, adding,

00:16:45.137 --> 00:16:46.605
"You know,
there's a debate going on.

00:16:46.605 --> 00:16:48.340
I'd rather be here,
spending time with you,

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:50.942
than watching the debate."
No one believes that.

00:16:50.942 --> 00:16:53.111
There's nothing Trump
would rather be doing

00:16:53.111 --> 00:16:55.046
than watching the debate
and tweeting dumb insults.

00:16:55.046 --> 00:16:56.348
He's probably shouting them out

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:58.016
in the middle of meetings
involuntarily.

00:16:58.016 --> 00:17:00.385
"So, anyway, we'd like
to cut tariffs on German cars.

00:17:00.385 --> 00:17:02.688
Sleepy Joe!"
[ Laughter ]

00:17:02.688 --> 00:17:04.523
'Course, another huge issue
in this campaign,

00:17:04.523 --> 00:17:06.658
one that deserves more time and
attention than it's been getting

00:17:06.658 --> 00:17:07.859
is the climate crisis.

00:17:07.859 --> 00:17:09.427
A lot of the candidates
have detailed plans

00:17:09.427 --> 00:17:10.696
to deal with this crisis.

00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:12.964
And then there's Hickenlooper,
a geologist,

00:17:12.964 --> 00:17:14.733
who found a way to mention
that he was a scientist

00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:16.268
not once but twice.

00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:17.836
-If you look at the
Green New Deal,

00:17:17.836 --> 00:17:19.604
which I admire
the sense of urgency

00:17:19.604 --> 00:17:21.707
and how important it is
to do climate change.

00:17:21.707 --> 00:17:22.875
I'm a scientist.

00:17:22.875 --> 00:17:26.044
I share the sense of urgency.
I'm a scientist.

00:17:26.044 --> 00:17:27.345
-All right, man,
if you have to say

00:17:27.345 --> 00:17:28.680
"I'm a scientist" once,
I'm on board,

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.748
but if you say it twice,
I'm skeptical.

00:17:30.748 --> 00:17:32.584
Your doctor doesn't come into
the exam room and say,

00:17:32.584 --> 00:17:35.220
"I'm a doctor.
Did you know I'm a doctor?"

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.888
Just say it once and move on.

00:17:36.888 --> 00:17:38.189
If I'm at a dinner party
and someone says

00:17:38.189 --> 00:17:40.191
"I'm a scientist" two times,
I'm faking an illness

00:17:40.191 --> 00:17:42.094
and getting the hell
out of there.

00:17:42.094 --> 00:17:44.195
Then later, moderator Chuck Todd
attempted to get an answer

00:17:44.195 --> 00:17:46.064
from the candidates on the
first issue they would tackle

00:17:46.064 --> 00:17:48.166
as president while some of them
bent the rules

00:17:48.166 --> 00:17:50.435
by listing multiple issues
or giving long answers.

00:17:50.435 --> 00:17:52.504
I'm not sure Biden
even understood the rules.

00:17:52.504 --> 00:17:53.938
-The first thing I would do

00:17:53.938 --> 00:17:57.576
is make sure
that we defeat Donald Trump.

00:17:57.576 --> 00:17:59.711
Period.
-Wait the first thing you do

00:17:59.711 --> 00:18:03.581
after you beat Donald Trump
is beat Donald Trump?

00:18:03.581 --> 00:18:04.983
"When I'm president, we'll hold

00:18:04.983 --> 00:18:06.852
a presidential election
every single day.

00:18:06.852 --> 00:18:08.887
I'll beat Donald Trump
on Monday,

00:18:08.887 --> 00:18:11.122
I'm gonna beat him again
on Tuesday.

00:18:11.122 --> 00:18:14.226
And then, when Wednesday rolls
around -- my time's up."

00:18:14.226 --> 00:18:20.799
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:24.503
Then -- Then, there was
Marianne Williamson,

00:18:24.503 --> 00:18:27.573
who rose up out of a lake under
a full moon to be at the debate.

00:18:27.573 --> 00:18:29.807
[ Laughter ]

00:18:29.807 --> 00:18:32.777
Williamson has been referred to
as Oprah's spiritual advisor,

00:18:32.777 --> 00:18:34.946
and when she was asked
what nation she would repair

00:18:34.946 --> 00:18:38.483
America's relationship with,
her answer was a little strange.

00:18:38.483 --> 00:18:39.918
-Well, one of
my first phone calls

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:43.355
would be to call the European
leaders and say we're back.

00:18:43.355 --> 00:18:45.724
-All right, that's --
Even if you're a friend,

00:18:45.724 --> 00:18:46.859
you don't want to hear that.

00:18:46.859 --> 00:18:48.359
It's like when
your in-laws come in town

00:18:48.359 --> 00:18:50.162
and stay at your place.
That's the first thing they say

00:18:50.162 --> 00:18:52.463
when they walk through
the door -- "We're back!

00:18:52.463 --> 00:18:54.700
And we will be moving
some furniture around."

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:55.833
[ Laughter ]

00:18:55.833 --> 00:18:57.402
Williamson didn't
get a lot of time tonight,

00:18:57.402 --> 00:18:59.170
and she's probably not gonna
be in the race for very long,

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:02.240
but we will always have her
closing statement from tonight,

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.876
which was less of a statement
and more of a reading

00:19:04.876 --> 00:19:06.678
from a one-person show titled

00:19:06.678 --> 00:19:09.047
"When you harness love,
love will win."

00:19:09.047 --> 00:19:11.082
-I have an idea
about Donald Trump.

00:19:11.082 --> 00:19:12.817
Donald Trump
is not going to be beaten

00:19:12.817 --> 00:19:14.853
just by insider politics talk.

00:19:14.853 --> 00:19:18.156
He's not going to be beaten
just by somebody who has plans.

00:19:18.156 --> 00:19:20.559
He's going to be beaten
by somebody who has an idea

00:19:20.559 --> 00:19:22.027
what this man has done.

00:19:22.027 --> 00:19:25.196
This man has reached into the
psyche of the American people

00:19:25.196 --> 00:19:27.999
and he has harnessed fear
for political purposes.

00:19:27.999 --> 00:19:30.702
So, Mr. President,
if you're listening,

00:19:30.702 --> 00:19:32.404
I want you to hear me, please.

00:19:32.404 --> 00:19:34.439
You have harnessed fear
for political purposes,

00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:36.574
and only love can cast that out.

00:19:36.574 --> 00:19:39.877
So I, sir, I have a feeling
you know what you're doing.

00:19:39.877 --> 00:19:43.047
I'm going to harness love
for political purposes.

00:19:43.047 --> 00:19:46.785
I will meet you on that field,
and, sir, love will win.

00:19:46.785 --> 00:19:50.455
[ Clapping ]

00:19:50.455 --> 00:19:57.629
[ Laughter ]

00:19:57.629 --> 00:20:00.098
-The four people who did not
qualify for these debates

00:20:00.098 --> 00:20:02.100
watched that and thought,
"What?"

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:04.169
[ Laughter ]

00:20:04.169 --> 00:20:06.471
Tonight's debates seemed a lot
feistier and more contentious

00:20:06.471 --> 00:20:08.005
than the first night,
but in both cases,

00:20:08.005 --> 00:20:10.208
the debates were issue-oriented
and policy-heavy.

00:20:10.208 --> 00:20:11.943
If Trump were watching,
I could only imagine

00:20:11.943 --> 00:20:14.746
that trying to follow all
the specific policy details

00:20:14.746 --> 00:20:17.115
left him feeling...
-Exhausted.

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:18.717
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:20:18.717 --> 00:20:22.921
[ Cheers and applause ]

